  "source": "The Swedish National Courts Administration",
  "note": [
    "All measures in this table concern cases within faster legal proceedings at district courts. Faster legal proceedings is an approach aimed at reducing the time between police intervention and resolution in court. The method covers crimes punishable by a maximum of three years of imprisonment, where the suspect is apprehended at the crime scene and involves offenses that the police can investigate on-site. Common offenses include the use and possession of narcotics, shoplifting, or driving without authorization.",
    "Only criminal cases with an indictment are included, but all cases involving minors are excluded."
  ]
